<title>UK: PaineWebber International wins June Reuter FX poll.</title>
<headline>PaineWebber International wins June Reuter FX poll.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>PaineWebber International in London beat 31 other banks and financial institutions from around the world to win the June Reuter foreign exchange poll.</p>
<p>PaineWebber improved on its strong performance in the May poll, where it came second.</p>
<p>The average divergence of Paine Webber's exchange rate predications from the actual rates taken at the European close on June 30 was just 0.6842 percent.</p>
<p>These reference closing rates were dollar/mark at 1.7435, dollar/yen at 114.52 and sterling/dollar at 1.6643.</p>
<p>In second place was Nikko Bank, London with a divergence of 0.9710 percent followed in third place by Commerzbank London with an average divergence of 1.0800 percent.</p>
<p>Overall, the percentage difference between the actual and forecast rates varied between 0.6842 and 3.1142 percent.</p>
